WEBVTT

00:05.490 --> 00:07.380
S-So, uh...

00:07.380 --> 00:10.520
We just gained a new friend today!

00:10.520 --> 00:12.890
This is Miss Lainie, 
daughter of Baron Cyan.

00:12.890 --> 00:14.350
Be nice to her, everyone!

00:19.940 --> 00:21.160
Uh...

00:23.610 --> 00:26.020
Oh, do forgive me. This calls for tea.

00:26.020 --> 00:27.580
Please wait a moment.

00:30.340 --> 00:31.510
Miss Lainie...

00:33.010 --> 00:35.590
I've been informed of your circumstances,

00:35.590 --> 00:39.910
and I have no feelings 
on the matter whatsoever.

00:42.160 --> 00:45.140
But I'm sure it still weighs on your mind.

00:45.140 --> 00:48.930
I'm not sure if I should 
condemn you or forgive you.

00:49.860 --> 00:51.640
It's too complicated.

00:51.640 --> 00:53.070
I'm sorry.

00:54.000 --> 00:58.230
Please, no! There's nothing 
you need to apologize for!

00:58.230 --> 01:00.030
It was all my fault!

01:00.820 --> 01:05.490
Miss Lainie, did you put me in that 
situation with malicious intentions?

01:05.490 --> 01:09.450
No, of course not! 
I never meant any such thing!

01:09.450 --> 01:14.660
In that case, I cannot hold you liable 
for the misfortune you were born with.

01:18.910 --> 01:21.030
You came here for your own reasons,

01:21.030 --> 01:23.430
which left you in need of help, correct?

01:24.010 --> 01:28.150
Which means I cannot very well 
slap away these hands.

03:04.530 --> 03:12.960
The Magical Revolution

03:04.530 --> 03:12.960
The Magical Revolution

03:04.530 --> 03:12.960
of the Reincarnated Princess and the Genius Young Lady

03:15.980 --> 03:17.540
So this is the girl I've heard about.

03:17.850 --> 03:20.520
You have magicite in your heart, do you?

03:21.620 --> 03:24.460
Tilty, Lainie is very sensitive.

03:24.460 --> 03:26.190
Try not to scare her.

03:26.610 --> 03:30.920
I hear you've captivated 
many young noblemen.

03:30.920 --> 03:32.930
How did...

03:34.360 --> 03:36.280
Huh? What's wrong?

03:37.170 --> 03:40.990
I see. If I hadn't been told in advance, 
I'd have been in trouble.

03:41.270 --> 03:45.440
Something made me feel 
sorry for her just now.

03:45.850 --> 03:50.030
Oh, so even people with broken 
personalities are affected, huh?

03:50.320 --> 03:53.040
Your fascination power 
really is amazing, Lainie!

03:53.040 --> 03:56.010
No, uh, I really have no idea what...

03:56.300 --> 03:59.210
So you're just activating it instinctively.

03:59.210 --> 04:01.680
It seems like inherent magic.

04:02.950 --> 04:05.390
Actually, I would bet...

04:05.390 --> 04:07.330
<i>that's</i> what it is, isn't it?

04:07.330 --> 04:10.310
Ah... You thought so too, huh?

04:11.010 --> 04:14.770
There aren't many people 
with magicite inside them.

04:14.770 --> 04:16.280
There's no doubt about it.

04:17.920 --> 04:19.690
I'm going to go get that thing.

04:27.790 --> 04:29.000
What is that?

04:29.570 --> 04:30.720
A forbidden text.

04:31.060 --> 04:31.900
A forbidden text?!

04:32.720 --> 04:35.370
Um, what is a forbidden text?

04:35.370 --> 04:38.640
They contain records of dangerous 
ideas and techniques,

04:38.640 --> 04:40.830
so reading them is forbidden.

04:40.830 --> 04:43.050
What is something like that doing here?

04:43.050 --> 04:46.140
Miss Anis brought it here. 
I don't remember when.

04:46.140 --> 04:47.930
Miss Anis...

04:47.930 --> 04:52.840
Uh, yeah, well... 
Let's put that aside for now.

04:53.200 --> 04:58.150
This is a collection of research notes 
left by a magician long, long ago.

04:59.170 --> 05:04.310
That magician's goal was the 
pursuit of the truth of magic.

05:04.660 --> 05:07.380
But the path he followed was endless.

05:07.380 --> 05:10.530
He would never reach its terminus, 
even after spending his life on it.

05:10.770 --> 05:13.660
So the magician decided to make 
up for his insufficient lifespan

05:13.660 --> 05:15.990
by using the lives of others.

05:16.510 --> 05:19.200
But... how?

05:19.200 --> 05:22.530
He used the power of magicite.

05:22.970 --> 05:26.190
Not like my magic medicine...

05:26.190 --> 05:28.180
but much more directly.

05:28.180 --> 05:31.270
He embedded magicite that he'd 
stolen directly into his own body

05:31.270 --> 05:33.600
and turned into a monster himself.

05:33.600 --> 05:36.550
And then he absorbed other people's lives.

05:36.910 --> 05:40.210
You ladies heard stories about it 
when you were little, didn't you?

05:40.210 --> 05:44.300
Stories of one who tricked humans 
to create more like him,

05:44.300 --> 05:47.310
who deceived people under 
the cover of night.

05:47.310 --> 05:50.210
The frightening monster 
spoken of in fairy tales...

05:50.750 --> 05:52.080
The vampire.

05:54.950 --> 05:57.670
Wait a moment. What are you talking about?

05:58.020 --> 06:01.880
Were we not just discussing 
the issue concerning Miss Lainie?

06:01.880 --> 06:06.350
They say anyone whose blood is sucked 
by a vampire becomes a vampire.

06:06.770 --> 06:11.060
But according to that book, 
it was actually a form of brainwashing.

06:11.060 --> 06:12.690
Brainwashing?

06:13.020 --> 06:18.660
In other words, the way a vampire 
would create more like him

06:18.660 --> 06:21.470
was to overwrite people's 
awareness to suit him.

06:21.470 --> 06:24.440
Our magician here had this thought:

06:24.440 --> 06:28.120
If he were to create plenty of extras 
who would inherit his ideology,

06:28.120 --> 06:31.910
and if one of them should arrive at 
the truth one day, that would suffice.

06:33.040 --> 06:34.420
How vile.

06:34.900 --> 06:38.340
A human using the power of magicite 
to manipulate people's thoughts...

06:38.750 --> 06:41.780
That's a story we've heard 
somewhere recently, isn't it?

06:41.780 --> 06:45.680
You mean I'm... a vampire?

06:48.960 --> 06:53.930
Oh, well... maybe not so much a vampire, 
but the descendant of one?

06:53.930 --> 06:58.150
The forbidden text says magicite within 
a person's body becomes hereditary,

06:58.150 --> 07:02.890
so most likely, your mother's 
mother's mother's... uh...

07:02.890 --> 07:06.640
I mean, if you could learn 
to control your own power,

07:06.640 --> 07:08.880
that would actually be amazing!

07:08.880 --> 07:10.560
Would it?

07:10.560 --> 07:14.180
That sounds interesting. Let's experimen—

07:14.180 --> 07:16.280
I mean, start training you right away.

07:16.550 --> 07:19.260
You want to control the 
magicite's power, don't you?

07:22.910 --> 07:25.870
The flow of mana within you has stagnated.

07:25.870 --> 07:28.180
Try doing exactly as I tell you.

07:28.180 --> 07:29.750
O-Okay.

07:38.920 --> 07:41.890
Okay. Not bad for your first time.

07:41.890 --> 07:43.860
We'll stop here for today.

07:43.860 --> 07:45.650
Thank you so much.

07:46.370 --> 07:48.600
Huh? Lainie, your eyes...

07:48.870 --> 07:49.600
Huh?

07:53.780 --> 07:57.520
H-Huh? What is this? My teeth...

07:57.520 --> 07:58.000
Your teeth?

07:58.370 --> 07:59.950
Whoa! Fangs!

07:59.950 --> 08:01.770
Well, Lainie?

08:01.770 --> 08:04.160
Do you feel like you can keep 
your fascination power in check?

08:04.450 --> 08:05.870
Oh... Yes!

08:05.870 --> 08:08.900
It's as if a fog I had within me 
just cleared up...

08:08.900 --> 08:13.130
I feel like I can clearly understand 
how to use my power now!

08:13.130 --> 08:16.150
The vampire magicite has been activated.

08:16.150 --> 08:17.600
Just as I thought.

08:17.870 --> 08:20.470
Everything's up to you now, Lainie.

08:20.470 --> 08:24.850
In her case, having magicite within her body 
had become a matter of course.

08:24.850 --> 08:28.530
Leaving it inactive within her 
was actually unhealthy.

08:28.530 --> 08:31.770
So now that the flow of mana 
within you has been activated,

08:29.550 --> 08:32.520
Those two are incredible.

08:31.770 --> 08:34.490
you should be able to control it 
at will from now on!

08:34.900 --> 08:37.990
It doesn't feel as if Lainie 
is doing anything right now.

08:37.990 --> 08:39.390
Which probably means...

08:40.180 --> 08:41.910
Euphie? Something wrong?

08:41.910 --> 08:44.130
No, nothing.

08:47.310 --> 08:50.930
Oh, right. I need to return 
this to the library.

08:50.930 --> 08:53.640
But I'd be bored going by myself.

08:53.640 --> 08:57.180
Miss Anis, I'm going to borrow 
Lady Euphyllia for a bit.

08:57.180 --> 08:58.080
Huh?

09:04.360 --> 09:05.260
Well...

09:06.640 --> 09:07.480
So?

09:07.730 --> 09:08.570
Huh?

09:08.930 --> 09:12.900
You were giving me quite 
a serious look back there.

09:13.230 --> 09:15.730
Is there something you'd like to say to me?

09:16.180 --> 09:17.860
Uh, not particularly...

09:18.970 --> 09:20.260
Are you jealous?

09:22.780 --> 09:26.760
Wait, what's her deal? 
Does she not even realize it?

09:26.760 --> 09:28.750
Is that how I looked?

09:29.060 --> 09:32.860
I'd like to know what else 
it could have looked like.

09:33.890 --> 09:35.420
I see.

09:35.900 --> 09:38.940
So I was jealous.

09:40.680 --> 09:43.600
Ugh, you're such a pain to deal with!

09:44.420 --> 09:46.800
Just what are you to Miss Anis?

09:47.460 --> 09:49.780
I'm... her assistant.

09:49.780 --> 09:53.520
I'm asking if you really see 
yourself as her assistant!

09:56.630 --> 09:59.030
Oh, don't make that face at me.

09:59.030 --> 10:01.670
You make it look like I'm the bad guy.

10:02.200 --> 10:05.080
The reason Miss Anis 
took you as her assistant

10:05.080 --> 10:08.130
was to restore your lost honor, was it not?

10:08.990 --> 10:13.080
She achieved that goal when she defeated 
the dragon, and on top of that,

10:13.080 --> 10:16.580
she went on to solve the mystery 
of Lainie and the strife she caused.

10:17.040 --> 10:20.540
So what reason do you have 
to continue being her assistant?

10:21.060 --> 10:23.010
I...

10:23.280 --> 10:26.900
It's not as if I'm trying 
to take away your role.

10:26.900 --> 10:32.260
I help Miss Anis because I find her 
magicology and magic tools fascinating,

10:32.260 --> 10:37.610
but I have no intention of going along with 
her foolish dream of becoming a magician.

10:38.070 --> 10:39.940
Really?

10:40.450 --> 10:42.400
Enough talking about me.

10:42.400 --> 10:45.050
I'm asking about <i>you</i>.

10:45.050 --> 10:47.360
What... about me?

10:47.360 --> 10:51.300
For instance, when Prince Algard 
becomes the next king,

10:51.300 --> 10:56.840
he might exile Miss Anis to the remote 
borderlands out of prejudice against her.

10:57.300 --> 10:59.560
Would you be able to accompany her?

11:01.800 --> 11:05.780
Of course. You can't give an immediate 
answer in the heat of the moment.

11:05.780 --> 11:10.560
What you say and do steers the fate 
of the Magenta family, after all.

11:12.100 --> 11:14.370
Miss Anis is a heretic.

11:14.370 --> 11:17.640
If you stand by her with half-hearted 
intentions, you'll regret it.

11:17.880 --> 11:19.920
I suggest you give it some serious thought.

11:22.830 --> 11:24.310
You're right.

11:34.470 --> 11:35.660
Come in.

11:38.710 --> 11:40.070
Miss Anis?

11:40.510 --> 11:41.920
Is something wrong?

11:41.920 --> 11:46.380
Huh? Oh, I don't really need anything...

11:46.630 --> 11:50.610
I just thought you seemed kind of down.

11:56.470 --> 11:58.560
What were you up to, Euphie?

11:59.320 --> 12:01.030
Well, I suppose...

12:01.030 --> 12:03.980
I was thinking about the future.

12:03.980 --> 12:06.050
What does that mean?

12:06.050 --> 12:09.260
Now that things have started to calm down,

12:09.260 --> 12:10.780
I was pondering what comes next.

12:12.140 --> 12:12.910
I see.

12:14.060 --> 12:16.680
I don't want to be half-hearted.

12:17.760 --> 12:19.370
Huh? What'd you say?

12:19.370 --> 12:21.190
Nothing at all.

12:23.650 --> 12:25.050
I was...

12:25.550 --> 12:31.020
I was just wondering what it is 
I really want to do.

12:31.610 --> 12:32.980
Did you find your answer?

12:35.290 --> 12:38.700
Why do you like magic so much?

12:39.610 --> 12:41.300
Well, that came out of nowhere.

12:41.300 --> 12:45.650
Hmm... All I can really say 
is because I like it.

12:46.410 --> 12:49.860
It's like being in love, I think. 
Not that I'd know.

12:51.590 --> 12:53.830
I want to fall in love like that, too.

12:56.520 --> 13:00.770
Hey, Euphie... Can I sleep in here tonight?

13:12.510 --> 13:14.100
U-Um...

13:19.040 --> 13:21.470
Miss Lainie, is something the matter?

13:21.880 --> 13:25.210
W-Well... I just, um...

13:25.700 --> 13:27.340
Can I...

13:27.970 --> 13:30.880
ask for your help again?

13:34.150 --> 13:35.290
I don't mind.

13:35.970 --> 13:37.010
Go ahead.

13:40.340 --> 13:41.930
An impulse to drink blood?

13:42.370 --> 13:43.320
Yes.

13:43.870 --> 13:48.090
Well, we did activate 
the magicite inside her.

13:48.090 --> 13:51.660
I think that makes her consume 
more mana than before.

13:52.060 --> 13:54.470
And when her body feels low on mana,

13:54.470 --> 13:57.760
it manifests in the form of 
an impulse to drink blood.

13:57.760 --> 13:59.560
Leave it to a vampire.

13:59.560 --> 14:03.740
So she can take the mana from other 
people's blood and make it her own.

14:03.740 --> 14:06.120
Have you let her drink any?

14:06.120 --> 14:07.830
Yes, Ilia has.

14:09.880 --> 14:15.370
We offered ours, too, but she told us 
to remember our positions.

14:15.370 --> 14:19.230
I am truly grateful to Miss Ilia.

14:20.610 --> 14:21.740
Princess.

14:22.520 --> 14:23.860
Oh, Ilia.

14:23.860 --> 14:27.190
Wait, what's wrong? Why the dark look?

14:27.190 --> 14:29.960
I just received this.

14:30.490 --> 14:32.270
It's from the Ministry of the Arcane.

14:33.060 --> 14:34.650
Ugh...

14:35.020 --> 14:36.590
What a pain.

14:36.920 --> 14:39.560
What did that garbage ministry say?

14:39.560 --> 14:43.530
They want Miss Anis to give a lecture.

14:43.760 --> 14:46.490
A lecture? That's amazing, Miss Anis!

14:47.010 --> 14:49.430
Oh, it's not that kind of thing.

14:49.720 --> 14:53.070
Basically, they want me to explain 
in front of a bunch of people

14:53.070 --> 14:55.400
what I plan to do with the 
materials from the dragon.

14:55.700 --> 14:57.360
Really?

15:01.960 --> 15:04.530
This is quite an aggressive letter.

15:04.860 --> 15:06.750
Right? Who wants anything to do with that?

15:06.750 --> 15:08.830
U-Um...

15:08.830 --> 15:12.460
The elites in the Ministry of 
the Arcane value tradition.

15:12.460 --> 15:15.730
They're not fond of the princess's 
magicology and magic tools.

15:15.970 --> 15:18.510
They say it's not in line 
with belief in the spirits,

15:18.510 --> 15:20.950
and that it'll be a negative 
influence on the people.

15:20.950 --> 15:26.470
They just want to find fault with me 
and take all my materials again.

15:27.440 --> 15:29.390
So what are you going to do?

15:29.390 --> 15:31.910
If you refuse to do the lecture 
because it's a hassle,

15:31.910 --> 15:36.560
it'll just raise undue suspicions 
and lead to more nasty rumors.

15:37.120 --> 15:38.980
And it won't just be you.

15:38.980 --> 15:41.830
All those close to you will suffer for it.

15:42.220 --> 15:43.640
I don't want that.

15:44.280 --> 15:45.290
That said, though...

15:45.780 --> 15:49.460
What should I do? 
That dragon's materials are valuable.

15:49.460 --> 15:52.190
I don't want to lose a single one of them.

15:53.700 --> 15:56.540
Okay! I'll just have to come up 
with a new product

15:56.540 --> 15:59.140
that'll convince even 
the Ministry of the Arcane!

15:59.410 --> 16:05.460
Would those people be convinced 
by anything a heretic princess says?

16:05.460 --> 16:06.520
Good point.

16:06.800 --> 16:10.030
Ugh, damn that Ministry of the Arcane!

16:10.430 --> 16:11.790
Miss Anis...

16:13.030 --> 16:15.440
Could you leave this matter to me?

16:15.440 --> 16:16.100
Huh?

16:40.000 --> 16:41.860
Greetings, ladies and gentlemen.

16:41.860 --> 16:45.570
I am Anisphia Wynn Palettia, 
your speaker for today.

16:48.130 --> 16:50.750
Oh, dear. Not a very receptive crowd.

16:51.040 --> 16:52.440
No kidding.

16:54.290 --> 16:57.900
I will now give my presentation 
explaining how I intend

16:57.900 --> 17:00.360
to use the materials 
from the dragon I defeated.

17:00.900 --> 17:01.840
However...

17:02.180 --> 17:06.290
Before I get started, I'd like you 
to take a look at this magic tool.

17:06.560 --> 17:10.000
A magic tool? Part of that shady 
business you call "magicology"?

17:10.000 --> 17:14.220
Isn't mimicry of magic 
sacrilege against the spirits?

17:14.490 --> 17:16.180
This is my Witch's Broom,

17:16.470 --> 17:20.380
a tool of flight that I invented 
using magicology.

17:20.760 --> 17:25.610
Using this, we can venture into the 
unexplored territory we know as the sky.

17:25.610 --> 17:30.570
Who would use such a thing other 
than the mad princess? Ridiculous!

17:30.570 --> 17:34.520
A princess who can't even use magic 
is truly unworthy of our time.

17:35.450 --> 17:36.480
<i>Wow...</i>

17:37.060 --> 17:40.450
<i>These old geezers aren't going to do 
anything but find fault with me.</i>

17:40.820 --> 17:41.910
Miss Anis.

17:48.190 --> 17:51.080
I am Princess Anisphia's assistant,

17:51.420 --> 17:53.290
Euphyllia Magenta.

17:53.580 --> 17:59.260
From this point onward, I will interject 
my own opinions as a magician.

17:59.550 --> 18:02.210
The genius daughter of Duke Magenta?

18:04.490 --> 18:06.490
As you all know,

18:06.490 --> 18:10.220
the power of flight is exceedingly 
difficult to both acquire and master.

18:10.220 --> 18:14.850
It has long been accepted that 
not just anyone can freely fly.

18:15.260 --> 18:18.670
But magic tools of flight make that possible.

18:19.060 --> 18:23.620
I say this as one who has seen 
Her Highness's research up close.

18:23.620 --> 18:25.890
Anyone can fly, eh?

18:25.890 --> 18:28.840
Hmm, how very intriguing.

18:28.840 --> 18:33.800
This Witch's Broom has already been put 
to practical use by its inventor.

18:34.160 --> 18:35.310
However...

18:36.080 --> 18:38.390
This shape is unacceptable.

18:38.390 --> 18:40.730
It seems to reflect its inventor's tastes,

18:40.730 --> 18:43.230
but it is problematic 
from a safety perspective.

18:43.230 --> 18:47.330
What? But brooms are what
witches are supposed to fly on.

18:47.330 --> 18:49.160
Where is that "normal"?

18:49.160 --> 18:54.620
Therefore, Her Highness set out 
to develop a more versatile magic tool.

18:55.580 --> 18:57.060
Please take a look at this.

18:59.330 --> 19:00.980
What is that?

19:00.980 --> 19:05.690
She calls it the "Airdra," representing 
the concept of flying like a dragon.

19:06.020 --> 19:10.060
With this, the pilot's body is as stable 
as if they were riding a horse,

19:10.060 --> 19:13.410
making it completely maneuverable and safe.

19:13.850 --> 19:16.710
If her research progresses 
to the point of mass production,

19:16.710 --> 19:19.640
our kingdom's transportation network 
will advance by leaps and bounds,

19:20.070 --> 19:24.230
bringing with it the potential 
for immense economic growth.

19:24.230 --> 19:26.180
If that's the case...

19:26.180 --> 19:27.850
We can't disregard this research.

19:29.300 --> 19:31.540
In order to produce the Airdra,

19:31.540 --> 19:34.070
the materials from the 
dragon are indispensable.

19:34.310 --> 19:35.760
Well, obviously.

19:34.530 --> 19:36.980
The Airdra's unique structure {eadora no tokui na kouzou wa}

19:35.760 --> 19:40.530
You came up with this tool specifically to 
stop the dragon materials from being taken.

19:36.980 --> 19:40.530
was inspired by the inherent 
magic that dragons use {doragon ga sono ... ukaseru tame ni mochiiru}

19:40.530 --> 19:43.710
to keep their enormous bodies airborne. {tokushu na koyuu ... eta mono desu}

19:40.790 --> 19:42.560
Shut up, Tilty.

19:43.710 --> 19:45.990
And as you all know, {mata minasama goshouchi no toori}

19:45.990 --> 19:51.140
different parts of a dragon act as catalysts 
for different types of magic, {doragon no ... narieru mono desu kara}

19:50.060 --> 19:52.160
It does make sense.

19:51.140 --> 19:55.200
so each of those materials 
plays a part in guaranteeing

19:53.090 --> 19:57.830
But in the face of the 
ancient faith in the spirits...

19:55.200 --> 19:57.360
the speed and safety of 
each part of the Airdra. {izure mo eadora kakubu ... kitai sarete orimasu}

19:58.070 --> 20:02.930
This concludes my explanation of the 
intended use of the dragon's materials.

20:04.040 --> 20:05.950
That wasn't too bad.

20:05.950 --> 20:08.350
Yeah. That's my Euphie.

20:08.350 --> 20:09.370
However...

20:10.130 --> 20:14.300
I fear that the Ministry 
of the Arcane may view

20:14.300 --> 20:19.500
such revolutionary research as sacrilege 
to the spirits and the gods.

20:19.500 --> 20:21.440
Wh-What?!

20:21.440 --> 20:23.910
It absolutely <i>is</i> sacrilege!

20:23.910 --> 20:24.920
Huh?

20:24.920 --> 20:27.360
Wow, you're pushing that far?

20:27.360 --> 20:29.320
No, I didn't ask her to!

20:29.640 --> 20:31.550
Oh, this was her own decision?

20:31.550 --> 20:33.540
Quite the assistant you've got there.

20:36.620 --> 20:40.140
Knowledge of the world, 
of reason, and of magic—

20:40.140 --> 20:43.710
from a combination of these, 
magicology is born.

20:43.710 --> 20:45.840
It is a field of study,

20:45.840 --> 20:49.420
not a practice intended to show 
disrespect to faith or tradition.

20:49.900 --> 20:52.090
It is true that the Her Highness's magicology

20:52.090 --> 20:58.890
is a bold concept unlike any presently known 
to us, and may appear incomprehensible.

20:58.890 --> 21:02.860
But that is simply an expression 
of respect toward the spirits.

21:04.650 --> 21:11.490
No, in fact, it came to be only 
<i>because</i> of that faith and tradition.

21:14.220 --> 21:17.760
It is not due to a lack of talent 
that Her Highness

21:17.760 --> 21:20.040
did not receive the spirits' blessing.

21:20.040 --> 21:24.220
It is because the spirits 
recognized the talents she has.

21:24.220 --> 21:26.890
That is what I want you all to understand.

21:26.890 --> 21:27.880
Euphie...

21:27.880 --> 21:33.600
I believe that now is the time 
for us to walk in step with change.

21:33.960 --> 21:36.570
I would like all of us to strive 
for the future together,

21:36.570 --> 21:39.820
along with the foundations 
with which we have come this far.

21:40.720 --> 21:46.450
My only wish is that today will be the 
first step toward that wonderful future.

21:58.910 --> 22:02.060
Thank you, Euphie.

